0..37 Comment "// This source defines a precategory."
38..40 Comment "//"
41..117 Comment "// `CatShape` has objects, a dependent hom type, identities and composition."
118..171 Comment "// Its unit and associativity laws are rewrite rules."
172..219 Comment "// It follows the HoTT book\'s Definition 9.1.1."
220..222 Comment "//"
223..300 Comment "// `SetoidCat` models the shape with types and functions. It checks every law"
301..366 Comment "// by conversion. One law can prove another law of the same type."
367..369 Comment "//"
370..400 Comment "// - see: #1510 — `CatShape`"
401..461 Comment "// - see: #452 — `identity_observed`, `composite_observed`"
462..485 Comment "// - cites: [HoTT-Book]"
486..488 Comment "//"
489..637 Comment "// [HoTT-Book]: https://homotopytypetheory.org/book/ \"The Univalent Foundations Program, Homotopy Type Theory: Univalent Foundations of Mathematics\""
639..715 Comment "/// `CatShape` defines a morphism sort indexed by two objects. It reads each"
716..774 Comment "/// law at the composite\'s objects, so the unit laws agree"
775..803 Comment "/// at `comp(id(a), id(a))`."
